==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|non|gem-pro|*gebaną||to give}}, from {{der|non|ine-pro|*gʰab(ʰ)-}}. Cognate with {{cog|ang|ġiefan}} ({{cog|en|give}}), {{cog|ofs|jeva}}, {{cog|osx|gevan}}, {{cog|odt|gevan}}, {{cog|goh|geban}}, {{cog|got|𐌲𐌹𐌱𐌰𐌽}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|non|/ˈɡevɑ/}}

===Verb===
{{non-verb|gaf|gáfu|gefinn}}

# {{lb|non|transitive}} to [[give]] something
# {{lb|non|ditransitive}} to give someone something
# ''gefa stað/staðar'' + dative: stop, cause to cease

====Conjugation====
{{non-conj-strong|class=5|gef|gaf|gáf|3i=gæf|gef}}

